> fA(x: real, y: real) = (x + y) ^ 2
> gA(x: real, y: real) = x ^ 2 + 2 * x * y + y ^ 2
> equiv fA gA
fA and gA are equal on the domain of fA (sampled, not proved; no SAT proof: a real value)
> fB(x: real, y: real) = (x + 3 * y) ^ 4
